index 0000000..f9ce9da
--- /dev/null
+++ b/runtime/clarus/atalk_68k.cla
@@ -0,0 +1,195 @@
+// Copyright 2026, Andrew C. Young <andrew@vaelen.org>
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
+
+// atalk_68k.cla: the native (68k) AppleTalk waist -- atalk_c.cla's twin,
+// same rtAtDev*/rtAdspDev*/rtLsnDev* names, one file spliced per lane
+// (the conn_68k.cla/conn_c.cla precedent).
+//
+// STUBS this task (2026-09-06 appletalk spec, Task 7). Every function
+// below reports "unavailable" (rtAtErrNoHost / 0 / false / ""), and this
+// module is spliced NOWHERE yet: drive.cla adds atalk.cla + atalk_c.cla to
+// the host lane only, and the 68k lane stays untouched (zero cg68k golden
+// churn). Task 9 replaces the BODIES -- no signature here moves.
+//
+// What Task 9 puts in these bodies (spec %5.2-%5.6, and the Task 1 probe
+// findings, which are binding):
+//   - .MPP/.ATP/.XPP/.DSP opened lazily with OpenDriver and never closed
+//     (Apple's warning: other processes may be using them); every call is
+//     a _Control with a csCode through toolbox/devices.cla.
+//   - EVERY per-slot parameter block must be fully re-zeroed before each
+//     reuse. A reused NBP parameter block hung the Mac in the probe --
+//     this is not a tidiness rule.
+//   - NBP registers the socket number VERBATIM, so a service writes its
+//     own ATP socket into the NTE before PRegisterName (which is why
+//     rtAtDevRegister takes `sock`), and a listener registers its own DDP
+//     socket (rtLsnDevSocket). A program's own address is read back out of
+//     the NTE after registerName.
+//   - Services: POpenATPSkt, PRegisterName (verify on), async PGetRequest
+//     into the slot's 578-byte buffer; PSendResponse async with the XO
+//     flag (a sync XO PSendResponse only completes on the requester's TRel
+//     or the 30 s release timer), which is what rtAtDevAtpRespBusy is for
+//     -- the pump does not re-arm PGetRequest while a response is still
+//     outstanding.
+//   - Browsers: async PLookupName, maxToGet 32, interval 8 (1 s), count 3;
+//     rtAtDevLookupName/-Addr parse the return buffer's tuples (the
